Menu="Utilities"
Type="xmenu"
Title="Drobo"
Icon="hdd-o"
Tag="hdd-o"
---
<?php
$cfg = parse_plugin_cfg('drobo');
function drobo_sel($cur, $val) { return $cur == $val ? ' selected' : ''; }
?>
<form markdown="1" name="drobo_settings" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#file" value="drobo/drobo.cfg">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/usr/local/emhttp/plugins/drobo/scripts/apply">

_(Check in the background every)_:
: <select name="INTERVAL">
  <option value="0"<?=drobo_sel($cfg['INTERVAL'],'0')?>>_(Off)_</option>
  <option value="5"<?=drobo_sel($cfg['INTERVAL'],'5')?>>5 _(minutes)_</option>
  <option value="15"<?=drobo_sel($cfg['INTERVAL'],'15')?>>15 _(minutes)_</option>
  <option value="30"<?=drobo_sel($cfg['INTERVAL'],'30')?>>30 _(minutes)_</option>
  <option value="60"<?=drobo_sel($cfg['INTERVAL'],'60')?>>_(Hour)_</option>
  </select>

<blockquote class="inline_help">
The check takes about a second and nothing stays running between checks. It only reads from the Drobo. Turn it off and the Main panel still works; you just won't get notifications.
</blockquote>

_(Send Unraid notifications)_:
: <select name="NOTIFY">
  <option value="yes"<?=drobo_sel($cfg['NOTIFY'],'yes')?>>_(Yes)_</option>
  <option value="no"<?=drobo_sel($cfg['NOTIFY'],'no')?>>_(No)_</option>
  </select>

<blockquote class="inline_help">
You get one notification when a problem starts (a failed or failing drive, a rebuild, low space, USB 2 speed, a read-only or unclean volume, or the Drobo disconnecting) and one when it clears. Where they go (browser, email, Discord…) is set in Settings → Notification Settings.
</blockquote>

_(Warn when the Drobo is this full)_:
: <input type="number" name="WARN_PCT" min="50" max="99" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['WARN_PCT'])?>" class="narrow"> %

_(Alert when the Drobo is this full)_:
: <input type="number" name="CRIT_PCT" min="50" max="100" value="<?=htmlspecialchars($cfg['CRIT_PCT'])?>" class="narrow"> %

<blockquote class="inline_help">
These use the Drobo's own count of protected space, not the free space Unraid shows for the volume. A Drobo turns its lights yellow at 85% and red at 95%, which are the defaults here.
</blockquote>

&nbsp;
: <input type="submit" value="_(Apply)_"><input type="button" value="_(Done)_" onclick="done()">
</form>

The status panel is on the **Main** tab.
